          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} Abstract Homotopy Theory and Generalized Sheaf Cohomology
              \.
          %h3#SliceAction Action on objects of the slice
          %p
            The free loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} slice (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on all objects of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
          %p
            Intuitively, the group structure comes from composition and inversion of loops. When the free loop space is expressed as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{S^1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogroup"} cogroup
            structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            is expressed as the pullback
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times_{X\times X} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi X
