          %h3#LoopsInBG
            Details for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            Let the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            its one-object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              We have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+groupoid"} loop groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Ad
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{L} \mathbf{B}G \simeq G//_{Ad} G
                    \\,,
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              of the adjoint action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on itself.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              We spell this out in full pedestrian detail, as a little exercise in computing
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %p
              We have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G^I = [I,\mathbf{B}G]
              – the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is the free groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{a \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} b\}
              on the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
              – which is (by the definition of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                    %mo \
                    %mo \
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}G^I = G\backslash \backslash G // G
            %p
              for the action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on itself, by
              %em inverse
              left and direct right multiplication separately: the naturality square of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              defining a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 2
                    %msubsup
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi g
                    %msub
