            %p
              which is naturally identified with a morphism in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Ad
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G//_{Ad} G
              of the adjoint action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on itself.
            %p This means that the inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Ad
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo \
                    %mo \
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G//_{Ad} G
                    \\stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow}
                    G\backslash\backslash(G \times G)//G
            %p
              given by this identification is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of groupoids
            %p
              So in conclusion we have that the free loop space object of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              of a group is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Ad
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{L} \mathbf{B}G \simeq G//_{Ad}G
                    \\,.
          %h3#chern_character Chern character
          %p
            We describe how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be realized in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of the free loop space object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
          %p
            Assume now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a nice category of smooth spaces, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            given by a group homomorphism to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            (in
            = succeed "):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho:G\to GL(n;\mathbb{C})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            could be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            itself and this morphism the identity.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            of the representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is invariant under conjugation in the group and so defnes a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Ad
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(\rho): G//_{Ad}G\to \mathbb {C}
            – a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+function"} class function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Ad
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}\mathbf{B}G \simeq G//_{Ad} G
            discussed above, this may be regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Tr(\rho(-)) : \mathcal{L}\mathbf{B}G\to \mathbb {C}
          %p
            on the free loop space of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X\to \mathbf{B}G
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            transgresses to a cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L} g : \mathcal{L}X \to \mathcal{L}\mathbf{B}G
          %p on the free loop space, by the functoriality of the free loop space object construction.
          %p
            The above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            of this cocycle is the composite morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Tr(\rho(\mathcal{L}g)) : \mathcal{L}X \to \mathcal{L} \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbb{C}
                  \\,,
          %p
            which by the
            = succeed "-invariance" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            is now
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{L}X,\mathbb{C})^{S^1_C}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The Hom-space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{L}X,\mathbb{C})
            is a model for the graded commutative algebra of complex-valued
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{L}X,\mathbb{C})^{S^1_C}
            is a model for closed forms and maps to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{dR}^\bullet(X)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            holds for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(X,\mathbb{R})
          %p
            In the case that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G=GL(\infty;\mathbb{C})
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            makes the above construction a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)\to H_{dR}(X)
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
          %p
            (
            %em to be completed…
            )
          %h3#isotropy_of_a_topos Isotropy of a topos
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropy+group+of+a+topos"} isotropy group of a topos
            is its free loop space object in the 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"}> loop space object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong free loop space object
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"}> loop space
                    ,
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+space"} derived loop space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+object"} suspension object
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
          %h2#References References
          %p
            Free loop space objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential graded algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
              %em Loop Spaces and Connections
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3636"}> arXiv
              )
          %p More information in the topological case is given in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
              = succeed "," do
                %em Crossed modules and the homotopy 2-type of a free loop space
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.5617"} arXiv
          %p
            which gives complete information on the 2-type of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            for a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which is the classifying space of a crossed module of groups. This generalises the above example of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} \mathbf{B}G
